odo-take/1
name: Greensleeves
by: Traditional English (16th century), the tune alone; written for odo by Claude
about: A slow tune in A minor, in three. It teaches the long-short rhythm (a dotted
about: note and a quick one), sliding up into a note, and vibrato on the long notes.
about: An octave below where it is usually written, so it sits in the middle of the Grid.
tempo: 84
meter: 3/4
key: A minor
controller: patrickreynolds/grid
settings: {"chromatic": 1, "slide": 1, "cols": 4}
sound: patrickreynolds/string-machine

